 Senate race is one of the closest contests of the cycle, pitting incumbent Republican Dan Sullivan against Democrat Mary Peltola. Recent polls from both partisan and independent pollsters show the race essentially tied, with several giving Peltola a small lead. Expert raters are split between Tossup and Lean D, and prediction markets now make Peltola a clear favorite.\n\nPeltola holds a large fundraising advantage and has drawn heavy outside opposition spending, while Sullivan benefits from incumbency in a state that leans Republican. The race may hinge on turnout, ranked-choice tabulation, and salmon and energy issues that resonate locally. A dramatic late development is the Justice Department's suit to block certification if Sullivan loses, adding unusual legal uncertainty to an already tight count.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5747, "margin": 0.87}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6955, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6995, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6965, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6035, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5728, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6289, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6364, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6246, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.603, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6381, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6392, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6364, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6469, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6459, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6429, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6784, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6123, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6534, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.6296, "margin": 2.2}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7064, "margin": 2.